## DESCRIPTION
## Calculus Two, Sequences
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Infinite sequences and series)
## DBsection(Limits of Sequences)
## Date(09/10/2018)
## Institution(Community College of Denver, Colorado Community College System)
## Author(Brittni Lorton)
## KEYWORDS('calculus', 'sequences', 'find terms of a sequence')

###########################
#  Initialization

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "PGcourse.pl",);

Context('Numeric');

$b = non_zero_random(-2, 2);

do {
    @a = (non_zero_random(-4, 4), non_zero_random(-4, 4));
} until ($a[0] != $a[1]);

push(@a, $a[ $_ - 1 ] + $b * $a[ $_ - 2 ]) for (2 .. 7);

BEGIN_PGML
Find the next six terms of the following sequence.

[`a_{n+2}=a_{n+1}[@ $b>0 ? '+' : '-' @] [@ abs($b)==1 ? "" : abs($b) @] a_n`],  [`a_1=[$a[0]], a_2=[$a[1]]`].

[`a_1=`][_]{$a[0]}

[`a_2=`][_]{$a[1]}

[`a_3=`][_]{$a[2]}

[`a_4=`][_]{$a[3]}

[`a_5=`][_]{$a[4]}

[`a_6=`][_]{$a[5]}

[`a_7=`][_]{$a[6]}

[`a_8=`][_]{$a[7]}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
This sequence is just formed term by term starting with the first two:

- [`a_1=[$a[0]]`]
- [`a_2=[$a[1]]`]
- [`a_3=[$a[1]][@ $b>0 ? '+' : '-' @][@ abs($b)==1 ? "" : abs($b) @] ([$a[0]]) = [$a[2]]`]
- [`a_4=[$a[2]][@ $b>0 ? '+' : '-' @][@ abs($b)==1 ? "" : abs($b) @] ([$a[1]]) = [$a[3]]`]
- [`a_5=[$a[3]][@ $b>0 ? '+' : '-' @][@ abs($b)==1 ? "" : abs($b) @] ([$a[2]]) = [$a[4]]`]
- [`a_6=[$a[4]][@ $b>0 ? '+' : '-' @][@ abs($b)==1 ? "" : abs($b) @] ([$a[3]]) = [$a[5]]`]
- [`a_7=[$a[5]][@ $b>0 ? '+' : '-' @][@ abs($b)==1 ? "" : abs($b) @] ([$a[4]]) = [$a[6]]`]
- [`a_8=[$a[6]][@ $b>0 ? '+' : '-' @][@ abs($b)==1 ? "" : abs($b) @] ([$a[5]]) = [$a[7]]`]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();
